def field(key,label,value,step='any'):
 return f'<label>{label}<input id="{key}" type="number" step="{step}" value="{value}"></label>'
lab='<div class="lab"><div class="eyebrow">INTERACTIVE / SYNTHETIC ASSUMPTIONS</div><h2>A bigger basket is not the same as better economics.</h2><p>Excluding-VAT planning model. Every buyer in each comparison chooses that one pack solely to isolate the arithmetic. No-purchase visitors remain included. This is not a forecast or a recommendation to change prices.</p><div class="fields">'+''.join([field('price','Normal unit price (R)',600),field('cost','Unit cost (R)',260),field('discount2','Two-pack discount (%)',15),field('discount3','Three-pack discount (%)',20),field('rateA','Control purchase rate (%)',3),field('rateB','Two-pack purchase rate (%)',1.8),field('visitors','Eligible visitors',1000,'1'),field('media','Media spend per variant (R)',5000)])+'</div><details><summary>Cost assumptions: edit packaging, delivery, fees and after-sale allowance</summary><div class="fields">'+''.join([field('pack1','Packaging / one (R)',20),field('pack2','Packaging / two (R)',25),field('pack3','Packaging / three (R)',30),field('ship1','Delivery / one (R)',70),field('ship2','Delivery / two (R)',80),field('ship3','Delivery / three (R)',100),field('fees','Payment fee (%)',3),field('allowance','Additional after-sale loss / unit (R)',12)])+'</div><p class="small">Shipping collected and fixed payment fee are zero in this illustration. The after-sale allowance must not duplicate refunds or other costs already recognised elsewhere. Fees are simplified scenario assumptions, not a provider quote.</p></details><div id="offerError" role="alert"></div><div id="offerResults" aria-live="polite"></div></div>'
views['offers']=lab+views['offers']
growth='<div class="lab"><div class="eyebrow">RECURRING SERVICE / SCENARIO, NOT FORECAST</div><h2>Separate the exit run rate from the year you actually bill.</h2><div class="fields">'+''.join([field('monthlyPrice','Monthly service price (R)',7500),field('newCustomers','New customers per month',2,'1'),field('churn','Monthly churn (%)',0),field('months','Months modelled',12,'1')])+'</div><p class="small">Starts with zero customers. Existing customers churn before new arrivals; every new customer pays a full month. No acquisition, service, tax, collection or overhead costs included. Fractional customers under churn are expected values.</p><div id="growthError" role="alert"></div><div id="growthResults" aria-live="polite"></div></div>'
views['growth']=growth+views['growth']
views['learning']='<div class="lab"><div class="eyebrow">DIAGNOSIS GATE / SYNTHETIC CASES</div><h2>Not every apparent result deserves a recommendation.</h2><label>Choose a case<select id="diagnosis"><option value="positive">Reviewed illustrative positive interval</option><option value="data">Incomplete tracking</option><option value="maturity">Outcomes still maturing</option><option value="organic">Organic / observational comparison</option><option value="srm">Allocation mismatch</option><option value="guardrail">Customer-service guardrail failed</option><option value="uncertain">Uncertain practical effect</option></select></label><div id="diagnosisResult"></div><p class="small">The code checks supplied flags. It does not verify identity, fit a statistical model or prove causality. All execution and publication outputs remain false.</p></div>'+views['learning']
